a mixed initialization state shall be undefined behaviour.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If the byte count of the original buffer slice is not a multiple of","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the stride of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"T"},{"text":", then the re-bound buffer is shorter","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"than the original buffer.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After executing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":", this method rebinds memory back to its original"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binding state. This can be unbound memory, or bound to a different type."}]},{"name":"Note","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The buffer slice’s start address must match the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"alignment of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"T"},{"type":"text","text":" (as reported by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MemoryLayout<T>.alignment"},{"type":"text","text":"). That is,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Int(bitPattern: base.baseAddress+startIndex) % MemoryLayout<T>.alignment","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"must equal zero."}]}],"type":"aside"},{"name":"Note","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A raw buffer slice may represent memory that has been bound to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a type. If that is the case, then "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"T"},{"type":"text","text":" must be layout compatible with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type to which the memory has been bound. This requirement does not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"apply if the raw buffer represents memory that has not been bound"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":